# NOTICE

Synthetic example exercising `Geometry3D_V2.Tin3D -> MultiPolygon`
(`convert/jsonfg.py`), the RULE #7 exception documented in
`docs/dev-notes/composite-surface3d-mapping.md` - kept here so the same
end-to-end example (and its JSON-FG output) is reproducible for external
tooling, not just inline in a pytest fixture string. Same template as
`tests/fixtures/solid3d_polyhedron/`/`tests/fixtures/curve3d_composite/`.

Copied unmodified from the swisstopo/interlis.ch model repositories -
`GEOMETRY3D_V2.ili` included, byte-for-byte
`https://models.geo.admin.ch/CH/CHBase_Part8_GEOMETRY3D_V2.ili`
(2023-10-18):

- `CHBase_Part1_GEOMETRY_V2.ili` - `https://models.geo.admin.ch/CH/`,
  VERSION "2025-07-30" (provides `GeometryCHLV95_V2.Coord3`, EPSG:2056).
- `CHBase_Part7_CONTEXT_V2.ili` - `https://models.geo.admin.ch/CH/`,
  VERSION "2021-01-06" (`ContextCHLV95_V2`).
- `Units-20120220.ili`, `CoordSys-20151124.ili` -
  `http://www.interlis.ch/models` (canonical base models, IMPORTS
  closure of `Geometry3D_V2`).

`GeologicalLayer_V1.ili` imports both `Geometry3D_V2` AND
`ContextCHLV95_V2`, same pattern as the other 2 `Geometry3D_V2` fixture
dirs.

**Synthetic, authored for this example** (not from any external source):
`GeologicalLayer_V1.ili` (a minimal `LayerBoundary` class with a
`Surface: Geometry3D_V2.Tin3D` attribute - the swisstopo "Basismodul 3D"
doc's own §1.2 application example, "Géologie : le type Tin3D peut être
utilisé pour des surfaces de séparation entre des couches géologiques")
and `layerboundary.xtf` (one `LayerBoundary`, two triangles sharing an
edge - an OPEN mesh, not a closed shell, exercising the case a
`Polyhedron` cannot represent).

`layerboundary.jsonfg.json` is the `interlis convert-jsonfg` output
against these fixtures (reference/golden output, not re-derived by a test
at import time) - validated with zero errors against the official
JSON-FG 1.0.0 schemas (`opengeospatial/ogc-feat-geo-json`, tag `v1.0.0`,
`core/schemas/*.json`) using the Python `jsonschema` library.

**No real corpus evidence for `Tin3D`/`SurfaceShell3D`/
`CompositeSurface3D` exists (0/71 real `.ili` files, 0/92 real `.xtf`
files, as of 2026-09-04)** - this whole fixture is synthetic and has not
been checked against a real producer's data. Revalidate against a real
example the day one surfaces.
